<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AVGOLD TO SPEND 92 MLN RAND ON EXPLORATION.</title>
<headline>AVGOLD TO SPEND 92 MLN RAND ON EXPLORATION.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African gold miner Avgold Limited has approved additional spending of approximately 92 million rand for further exploration at its Target and Sun areas, the company said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Work will include a 3-D seismic survey, an additional 15 boreholes and 17 long deflections from existing boreholes.</p>
<p>The work is part of the company's project to accelerate development of its northern Free State gold projects, Avgold said.</p>
<p>It said drilling would start this month and completion was expected in August 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
